#
#	Since sometimes Apache isn't properly configured to view the
#	proper PHP script, we used to do this instead, but only if PHP5 is
#	installed and working properly.
#
#	Deferred item 24 (final wave, CWE-16 hygiene): the test used to name
#	`mod_php5.c`, a module that only exists on PHP 5.x. On PHP 7/8 the Apache
#	module registers as `mod_php.c` (`php_module`), so the block never matched
#	and never ran. Measured on this harness (PHP 8.3.35 / Apache 2.4.68): a
#	probe directory whose .htaccess wrapped `Require all denied` in
#	`<IfModule mod_php5.c>` answered HTTP 200 - the block was not evaluated -
#	while the same probe with `<IfModule mod_php.c>` answered 403.
#
#	The block is therefore inert and is now commented out so it does not read
#	as a live control. The directory index is set by the server configuration
#	(doc/freemed.apache.conf:9 - `DirectoryIndex index.php index.html ...`),
#	which is where an operator should look; a DirectoryIndex directive here
#	would REPLACE that list for the whole tree rather than add to it.
#
#<IfModule mod_php.c>
#	DirectoryIndex index.php
#</IfModule>
